  "question": {
    "text": "The area of the region bounded by the curves $x$ $=y^2-2$ and $x=y$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "42aSp",
      "text": "$\\frac{9}{4}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "v4FUc",
      "text": "$9$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "rWAQj",
      "text": "$\\frac{9}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "GrYcf",
      "text": "$\\frac{9}{7}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Given, $x=y^2-2$ and $x=y$.\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/cC7sDC8y5-9eTwJAFhGUAwnXFfpFeZcB1zZr6N7rFhM.original.fullsize.png\"/>\nOn solving, $x=y^2-2$ and $x=y$, we get $(-1,-1)$ and $(2,2)$.\nArea of the shaded region,\n$\\begin{aligned}\n& A=\\int_{-1}^2 y d y-\\int_{-1}^2\\left(y^2-2\\right) d y \\\\\n& =\\left[\\frac{y^2}{2}-\\frac{y^3}{3}+2 y\\right]_{-1}^2=\\left(\\frac{4}{2}-\\frac{8}{3}+4\\right)-\\left(\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{3}-2\\right) \\\\\n& =\\frac{10}{3}+\\frac{7}{6}=\\frac{27}{6}=\\frac{9}{2} .\n\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
